Subject: Harden Fil-C compile-time rejections and enable permanent IR verification
Upstream-Base: llvmorg-23.1.6 (5b10d2d74929eae78912771222c9855af97496f4)
Fil-C-Head: cede3de02b42b58a14acc9ce39c9894ab952a915 (branch deluge)

In Release builds with LLVM_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS=OFF, llvm_unreachable() and
assert() compile away into UB or no-ops. This patch hardens all user-input-
reachable rejections and keeps module IR verification active in Release builds:

- clang/lib/Sema/SemaChecking.cpp: Reject __builtin_setjmp and __builtin_longjmp
  directly in Sema with err_builtin_setjmp_unsupported / err_builtin_longjmp_unsupported.
- llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FilPizlonator.cpp:
  * Emit clean Clang backend diagnostics via M.getContext().emitError(...) and
    bail out cleanly (no crash dump / bug-report banner) for user-reachable
    rejections: unsupported module inline asm, non-zero pointer address spaces,
    unlowered indirectbr, defining reserved pass-through functions, and
    incompatible setjmp/_setjmp/sigsetjmp prototypes.
  * Replace remaining user-reachable unreachable/assert checks (eh.sjlj
    intrinsics, CallBrInst fallback, SEH funclet instructions, scalable vectors,
    SafeAdd64/SafeMul64 64-bit layout overflow checks, unsupported pointer
    atomicrmw, linkage, ConstantExpr, unknown instruction) with
    report_fatal_error(..., /*GenCrashDiag=*/false).
  * After emitting noreturn filc_error for CallBrInst (asm goto) or unhandled
    intrinsics, erase the unlowered instruction (replacing CallBrInst with
    UnreachableInst after updating successor PHIs, and RAUWing non-void results
    with a dummy LoadInst) so no unlowered OldF arguments survive verification.
  * Always run verifyModule(M, &errs()) after FilPizlonatorPass (even in Release
    builds with LLVM_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS=OFF) so invalid IR is caught immediately
    with full verifier diagnostics instead of silently miscompiling.
- clang/lib/CodeGen/CGRecordLayoutBuilder.cpp & clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp:
  Replace user-reachable non-zero address space, scalable vector, GCC job
  refusal, and linker version-script parse/EOF/write unreachables with
  report_fatal_error(..., /*GenCrashDiag=*/false).

---
